@startuml modbusBusInstallation5C88
' ============================================================
' Greenhouse Ventilation Controller
' UML deployment diagram: the Modbus RS485 bus as installed at
' Herenboeren Willemshoeve (5C88)
'
' Layout, lengths and terminator positions: the operator,
' 2026-10-30. Board details: hardware/ModBusRS485*CableJunction/pcb.
' Controller details: design/technicalHardwareDesignSpecification.md 4.3.
' PCB types follow from each box's connections.
' ============================================================

title Modbus RS485 bus as installed at Herenboeren Willemshoeve (5C88)\nUML deployment diagram, 2026-10-31

left to right direction
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam node {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #444444
  FontSize 12
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #F0F4FF
  BorderColor #5566AA
}

rectangle "Outdoors, 6 m mast" <<location>> as MAST {
  node "**SenseCAP S200**\nwind sensor\nModbus addr **44**" <<device>> as S200
  node "**Junction box 1**\nend PCB, SingleCableJunction\n**TERMINATOR 1: 120 Ω**\nR1 enabled by JP3" <<PCB>> as BOX1
}

rectangle "Controller position, greenhouse wall" <<location>> as CTRLPOS {
  node "**Junction box 2**\nT PCB, DualCableJunction\nno terminator: JP9, JP10 open" <<PCB>> as BOX2
  node "**Controller 5C88** (bus master)\nLOLIN S3, SIT65HVD08P\nSM712 TVS on A and B\nR19, R20: 20 kΩ idle bias\nR21: 120 Ω, **disabled** (J8 off)" <<device>> as CTRL
}

rectangle "T/RH position, greenhouse" <<location>> as THPOS {
  node "**Junction box 3**\nT PCB, DualCableJunction\nno terminator: JP9, JP10 open" <<PCB>> as BOX3
  node "**FG6485A**\ntemperature and humidity\nModbus addr **1**\n**TERMINATOR 2: about 120 Ω**\nsensor side of the stub, measured\nnot in the spare FG6485A" <<device>> as FG
}

rectangle "M3 window" <<location>> as M3POS {
  node "**Wire encoder board**\nM3 window position sensor\nModbus addr **40**\nno stub, cable ends here\n120 Ω **disabled** 2026-10-30" <<device>> as ENC
}

S200 -- BOX1 : stub\n2 m
BOX1 -- BOX2 : <<RS485>>\n10 m
BOX2 -- CTRL : stub
BOX2 -- BOX3 : <<RS485>>\n6 m
BOX3 -- FG : stub\nabout 1 m
BOX3 -- ENC : <<RS485>>\n6 m

legend bottom
  **Bus:** Modbus RTU, 9600 baud 8N1, RS485 half duplex. Slaves are addresses 1, 40 and 44. Trunk 22 m from box 1 to the window sensor, plus the stubs.
  **Termination:** two 120 Ω, at box 1 and at the T/RH, which sits mid-bus. The window sensor's end has none.
  **Measured 2026-10-31:** A to B reads 60 Ω with all sensors connected and 120 Ω with the FG6485A out. The spare FG6485A alone reads 150 kΩ. No FG6485A document mentions a resistor.
  **Cable between junction PCBs:** RJ45 (215877-1). 24 V on pins 4, 5 and GND on pins 7, 8. A and B on pins 1, 2 or 3, 6, set by the pair selector.
  **End PCB, SingleCableJunction:** one RJ45, one stub (J2). 120 Ω R1 enabled by JP3, which is CLOSED as made: terminated unless the trace is cut.
  **T PCB, DualCableJunction:** two RJ45, two stubs, joined by JP7 and JP8 (closed as made). 120 Ω R1 and R2 enabled by JP9 and JP10, OPEN as made: not terminated.
  **Bias:** 20 kΩ pairs at the controller (R19, R20) and, per its schematic, on the wire encoder board (R3, R2): about 10 mV idle at 60 Ω.
endlegend

@enduml
